<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <!-- Framework, language version and shared metadata come from Directory.Build.props. -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
        <GeneratePackageOnBuild>False</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
        <Description>A static website generator for C# developers. It enables entire websites to be built using C#. Custom templates are supported. See the documentation to learn how to create them.</Description>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
        <PackageTags>StatiC#; StatiCSharp; staticsharp; Staticsharp; StatiCsharp; static; website; generator;</PackageTags>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<PackageIcon>Icon.png</PackageIcon>
		<Title>StatiC#</Title>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>Version 1.0.0 rewrites the public API and fixes a number of long-standing defects.

- Requires .NET 10.
- Fluent configuration: Website.Create(...).With... and WebsiteManager.For(...).With...MakeAsync(). The old constructors and settable properties are gone.
- A site's url is the single answer to where it is written, so a link and the file behind it cannot disagree. Every segment is normalized: a folder named "My Section" is served from /my-section. A path entry in the front matter can no longer write outside the output directory.
- Meta data is treated as plain text and encoded on output, so a quote in a title or author name no longer breaks the page head.
- Dates are read as ISO 8601 and written the way the website's language writes them - arrangement as well as wording - independent of the machine running the generator. Themes can use StatiCSharp.Tools.DateText.
- Output is written incrementally by default: unchanged files are left alone, and files the generator did not produce are removed. WithPreservedOutput names exceptions; .git, .nojekyll and CNAME are always kept.
- The default theme's navigation says a section's title instead of its folder name, in the order the sections were declared, and no longer links a section that has no index.md.
- A website is configuration only. Index, Pages and Sections are no longer on IWebsite: reading returns its result instead of filling the website, so one website can be generated any number of times.
- The public interfaces hand out read-only collections, so a theme cannot write into what it is rendering.
- Themes get a RenderContext: every IHtmlFactory method is handed the website's configuration and all of its content, so a theme no longer takes the website in its constructor and can build a navigation, a sitemap or a tag cloud.
- Markdig raised to 1.4.0.

See the readme for the full upgrade notes.</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
    </PropertyGroup>

	<!-- Default Resources-->
    <ItemGroup>
        <None Remove="DefaultResources/styles.css" />
	    <None Remove="DefaultResources/favicon.png" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
		<Content Include="DefaultResources/default-theme/styles.css" pack="true">
			<PackageCopyToOutput>true</PackageCopyToOutput>
			<CopyToOutputDirectory>Always</CopyToOutputDirectory>
		</Content>
		
		<Content Include="DefaultResources/favicon.png" pack="true">
			<PackageCopyToOutput>true</PackageCopyToOutput>
			<CopyToOutputDirectory>Always</CopyToOutputDirectory>
		</Content>
    </ItemGroup>

	<!-- Most of the site model is internal, so the tests reach it through here. -->
    <ItemGroup>
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="StatiCSharp.Tests" />
    </ItemGroup>

	<!-- Markdig Markdown Reader -->
    <ItemGroup>
        <PackageReference Include="Markdig" Version="1.4.0" />
    </ItemGroup>
	
	<!-- NuGet -->
    <ItemGroup>
        <None Include="../../LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
        <None Include="../../Packaging/Images/Icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
        <None Include="../../Packaging/README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>
